      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the language is a \"factual reflection\" of its *time*, it should not be mistaken for objective truth; it is a reflection of a deeply biased worldview. You can guide students to distinguish between historical documentation and endorsement, arguing that while the text authentically captures the *mindset* of colonialism, that mindset itself is morally flawed. The value of the book lies precisely in its ability to expose and critique that very mindset, rather than simply chronicling its supposed 'rawness.' Therefore, the \"reality\" it depicts is one that scholars are obligated to critique.",
